      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T17:08:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be done before atomic_read_clear of tasks_waiting_on_reset?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 448,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "163a99ed92fed406fd038bf585b00ae3c238eb0e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21f0ec0b_a7792880",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 448,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T18:13:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since we are calling the handle_device_access() method it doesn\u0027t actually matter if we call this before or after clearing tasks_waiting_on_reset. We still do want to do this before we notify the waiting tasks below.\n\nIf we called pd_device_accessed() method instead; the call would have to be called after clearing the waiting tasks variable otherwise we would also ignore that call (line 383)\n\nEven though I am calling handle_device_access directly instead of pd_device_access, I thought it would be better to use the more constrained call sequence in case it was updated later.",
      "parentUuid": "a4b1edd4_b1225f6c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 448,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "163a99ed92fed406fd038bf585b00ae3c238eb0e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b64b907_db480a82",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 448,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T18:29:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reason why I thought handle_device_access should be moved up before clearing the state of tasks_waiting_on_reset is to avoid the following race:\n\n1. PD task - Clears tasks_waiting_on_reset\n2. X task - Calls pd_device_in_low_power --\u003e true and so calls pd_wait_for_wakeup thus setting tasks_waiting_on_reset for task X\n3. PD task - Calls wake event for all waiting tasks in #1 which did not include task X.",
      "parentUuid": "21f0ec0b_a7792880",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 448,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "163a99ed92fed406fd038bf585b00ae3c238eb0e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f361a80d_33e733d0",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 448,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T19:20:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we move the handle_device_access method (which makes pd_device_in_low_power return false) before clearing the tasks_waiting_on_reset, then we can still get into the scenario you described\n\n1. Task X checks low power mode -\u003e true\n2. PD Task clears low power mode\n3. PD Task clears waiting tasks\n4. Task X calls pd_wait_for_wakeup (and adds itself to waiting list)\n\n\nIn both cases, Task X misses this round of wake up and has to wait for the next round. The downside of both of these scenarios is that the TCPC will get reset twice pretty quickly; I am tempted to add code to prevent the double reset case, but I am concerned it will add unnecessary complexity for something that doesn\u0027t happen often and doesn\u0027t really have negative consequences (other than being wrong from a purity standpoint). Thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "2b64b907_db480a82",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 448,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "163a99ed92fed406fd038bf585b00ae3c238eb0e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "024a833f_c443efc5",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 448,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T19:30:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is true. I was just thinking about the same thing i.e. if we need to make the pd_device_in_low_power and pd_wait_for_wakeup a single call so that there is no race. But as you mentioned it could end up adding unnecessary complexity.\n\nOkay lets push this in and we can revisit this again if the double reset is an issue. Can you please add a comment here indicating that there could be a double reset scenario here in case there is a race?",
      "parentUuid": "f361a80d_33e733d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 448,
        "endChar": 28
      },
